{:edb/db-before-t 2176 :edb/db-after-t 2177 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535489 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:05:41.485Z" 13194139535489 true] [17592186064081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186351708 13194139535489 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186351694 13194139535489 true] [17592186064082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186351701 13194139535489 true] [17592186351694 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351695 13194139535489 true] [17592186351694 1089 "q-21521" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351694 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535489 true] [17592186351694 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+24x-36.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(4)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(4)>0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=4$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=4$" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351694 1113 #uuid "926334df-0b1b-522b-8706-62f62f0aec44" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351694 1145 "We're given that $x=4$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)=-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{2}+24x-36,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}+24.\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=-3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(4) & =-3(4) \\\\  & =-12<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351696 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351697 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351698 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351699 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351700 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1041 "selection" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351698 13194139535489 true] [17592186351695 1110 #uuid "a6fbe6af-8468-576c-a07f-7773a87a6606" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351696 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351696 1111 #uuid "32f938ad-353c-563a-bb28-434637d997ca" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351697 1034 "I only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351697 1111 #uuid "18f053ff-a1fe-5622-9c8d-98932373bb88" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351698 1034 "III only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351698 1111 #uuid "15f0c010-1361-5997-9f40-1d109164d664" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351699 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351699 1111 #uuid "a33c956c-2e8d-59a8-94af-bad5756927e6" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351700 1034 "II only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351700 1111 #uuid "211a6fa5-53b7-5ba5-97e5-e0ef073485fb" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351701 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351702 13194139535489 true] [17592186351701 1089 "q-22580" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351701 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535489 true] [17592186351701 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Given that ${f}^{′}(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})>0$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative minimum at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$\n- $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351701 1113 #uuid "ab4d3059-294a-5af3-acf8-ea96870985be" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351701 1145 "We're given that $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is a stationary point of $f(x).$ We will use the second derivative test to classify this stationary point.\n\nCalculating the first derivative for the function $f(x)={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-{e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\n$$\n\nCalculating the second derivative, we get \n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)={e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-{e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =2{e}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi /4}(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /4}<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative is negative, we conclude that $f(x)$ has a relative maximum at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351703 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351704 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351705 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351706 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351707 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1041 "selection" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351705 13194139535489 true] [17592186351702 1110 #uuid "82a60489-ba67-56dc-bc34-5c843f940afd" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351703 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351703 1111 #uuid "217bd976-896b-5452-b1ad-a3a847da13dd" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351704 1034 "I only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351704 1111 #uuid "782bd92e-d7ba-5a6d-93ac-0b1097dbfaab" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351705 1034 "III only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351705 1111 #uuid "506869c7-6597-5de4-9a29-a8668746b2b6" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351706 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351706 1111 #uuid "43bd9121-1122-5bf5-bdfa-92ba248aa110" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351707 1034 "II only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351707 1111 #uuid "0977ef3a-d411-5be6-a292-8ee01ebcd3b8" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351708 1017 #edb/ref 17592186351709 13194139535489 true] [17592186351708 1089 "q-2471" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351708 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535489 true] [17592186351708 1100 "For the function $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-10,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${f}^{″}(0)>0$\n- $x=0$ is a relative maximum of $f(x)$\n- ${f}^{″}(-2)<0$\n- $x=-2$ is a relative minimum of $f(x)$" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351708 1113 #uuid "8564b8fc-7dae-5753-9233-dc13c5a14ab8" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351708 1145 "We need to identify the critical points. Then, we then need to classify them using the second derivative test.\n\nFirst, we need to identify the critical points. Differentiating $f(x)=5{x}^{3}+15{x}^{2}-10,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=15{x}^{2}+30x,\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15{x}^{2}+30x & =0 \\\\ 15x(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have critical points at $x=0,-2.$\n\nNext, we need to determine the sign of ${f}^{″}(x)$ at the critical points. Computing ${f}^{″}(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=30x+30,\n$$\n\nand evaluating ${f}^{″}(x)$ at each critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(0) & =30>0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(-2) & =-30<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that:\n\n- Statements I is true while statement II is false. The second derivative is positive at $x=0,$ so this is a relative minimum of $f(x).$\n\n- Statements III is true while statement VI is false. The second derivative is negative at $x=-2,$ so this is a relative maximum of $f(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351710 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351711 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351712 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351713 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186351714 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1041 "selection" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1104 #edb/ref 17592186351710 13194139535489 true] [17592186351709 1110 #uuid "ef8313ce-ae4d-5118-8cbe-c50971c859f6" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351710 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351710 1111 #uuid "4ebe0146-c584-5f47-8010-3c8379701446" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351711 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351711 1111 #uuid "b563e8e5-dc73-5e8f-95c5-d976e23ee2ba" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351712 1034 "III only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351712 1111 #uuid "e7dfa8c7-cab8-592d-9377-28775914c156" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351713 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351713 1111 #uuid "eda0df5e-de01-5e8a-a6e5-0b7767ed77e8" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351714 1034 "I, II, III, and IV" 13194139535489 true] [17592186351714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535489 true] [17592186351714 1111 #uuid "0b4db8c8-7f26-5736-b2f9-10180aa560ba" 13194139535489 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-21521" 17592186351694 "q-21521/selection" 17592186351695 "q-21521/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" 17592186351696 "q-21521/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0a